			<div class="content" id="post-content-4200737">
									

<p>So the idea here is cool and chunks of this are decent, but there are a few issues I have with this. First up, the idea that they got this from the Wanderers Library irks me somewhat. The Library is extra-dimensional, and the idea that the Foundation would start raiding other realities to start looking for stuff to contain is a slippery slope that I'm not sure they'd go down, especially in the specific case of the library. There are probably 1000s of things in there the Foundation would want to contain if given the chance.</p>
<p>Second, the entire section with the ink analysis is massively overblown. We don't really need to know all those percentages or anything - you could just say &quot;the ink was analysed and we've determined how many entries are original&quot; or something. Thirdly, you're really missing an opportunity here only having a single example at the end. You could have had 3 or 4 examples easily, I feel, and ended on the santa claus note. An entry from the Russian and Japanese books would have been neat.</p>

							</div>

								
					
